Budget:
- Current stated cap in PROJECT.md/HANDOFF = 7200. Budget directive requests 6000. It's not an approval. Cap remains 7200 for any plan until operator formally applies change. 
- If applied: all-Reference 6980 > 6000 (over by 980); cannot meet R6 with all-Reference. Minimum all-Reference cost fixed: 3*1800=5400 + 1280 fixed + 300 battery = 6980. No cheaper Reference. So design change needed.
- Mixed Echo-S1/Reference-S2/S3 = 5780, fits 6000 with 220 headroom, but R3 not established at S1 edges; requires Echo verification at 35-44 & 61-65 RH and 12-26C, cross-model calibration, unified time base, raw units. Also no same-model spare. This is fallback/conditional, not approved.
- All-Echo = 3540 but field validation shows +9 to +12 µg/m3 at 85-95% RH, so fails R3 at S2/S3; no validated correction. Reject as primary even under budget pressure.
- So budget reduction and R3/R1/R2 unchanged cannot be simultaneously satisfied by any currently supported design; need operator decision: either keep 7200 (all-Reference) or approve mixed with verification (if S1 passes), or accept infeasibility. Also budget change doesn't solve schedule (References still 4-day lead). All-Echo could meet schedule but not R3 at S2/S3.

Evidence:
- Field validation candidate:
  - Units converted; table.
  - Echo F01-F02 at 45/60 RH errors +1.0/+1.2 (consistent with lab); F03-F05 at 85/90/95 RH errors +9.0/+11.0/+12.0 -> large positive bias, far above ±3. No valid humidity correction; not usable at S2 (80-95) or S3 (70-90) without new evidence/correction.
  - Reference F06-F08 at 85/90/95 RH errors +0.6/+0.8/-0.8 -> max abs 0.8, consistent with lab and within ±3 at those points. Extends coverage to 85% but still gaps at 80-84, 70-74, 76-84, S1 35-44/46-65, temperatures 9-17/23-26.
  - n=8, single field event, not long-term, not accepted. Candidate only.
- This new evidence would, if accepted, strengthen the rejection of Echo at high RH and support Reference. But doesn't solve budget or schedule.

Newsletter:
- No change; not a source; no action.

